{
  "analysis": "Doom is booting successfully now - it prints the initialization messages, finds and loads doom.wad, and gets to R_Init. However, it fails on Z_Malloc trying to allocate 25MB, which exceeds the 600000-byte zone. The zone size calculation is likely based on a memory query or default that isn't working correctly in the VM. I need to inspect how the zone size is determined in i_system.c and z_zone.c.",
  "plan": "Inspect i_system.c and z_zone.c to understand how the zone memory size is calculated. It may need a syscall to return available memory, or there may be a command-line parameter. Then I'll patch the VM or provide the right arguments to fix the zone size.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"ZONE\\\\|zone\\\\|memory\\\\|Z_Malloc\\\\|malloc\\\\|MEMSIZE\\\\|memsize\\\\|DEFAULT_MEM\" /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/i_system.c | head -40\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"ZONE\\\\|zone\\\\|memory\\\\|Z_Malloc\\\\|malloc\\\\|MEMSIZE\\\\|memsize\\\\|DEFAULT_MEM\\\\|prefs\" /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/z_zone.c | head -40\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"mb\\\\|memory\\\\|mem\\\\|zone\\\\|-mem\\\\|DEFAULT\\\\|ZONE_SIZE\\\\|zone_size\\\\|Z_Init\" /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/i_system.c /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/z_zone.c | head -60\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,120p' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/i_system.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
